    "blurb": "relational dimensioning showcase",
    "source": "# TO-252 / DPAK — relational dimensioning showcase.\n#\n# Vendor drawings for this package are a classic offset maze: the pins are\n# dimensioned center-to-center, the tab from the pin row by its NEAR EDGE,\n# and the body from the pin row again. Enter each number exactly the way the\n# drawing measured it; never convert to a common origin by hand.\n\nfootprint \"TO-252\" {\n  description \"DPAK, 2 leads + tab\"\n  refdes \"Q\"\n\n  pad 1 rect 1.1 x 1.6\n  pad 3 rect 1.1 x 1.6\n  pad 2 rect 5.5 x 6.2                       # the tab (drain)\n\n  pad 3 is 4.56 right of pad 1               # center-to-center across the pin row\n  pad 2 is centered between pad 1 and pad 3 horizontally\n  pad 2 inner is 1.9 above pad 1             # tab's near edge, 1.9 above pin centers\n\n  # equivalently, symmetric about the centerline:\n  #   pad 3 mirrors pad 1 across y\n  #   pitch pad 1 to pad 3 is 4.56\n\n  body 6.6 x 6.1 x 2.3\n  body bottom is 1.1 above pad 1             # body edge, also given from the pin row\n  body is centered on pad 2 horizontally     # else §9.2's weak cross-axis rule aligns it with pad 1\n  pin1 none\n}\n"
