    "title": "QFN library",
    "blurb": "one template, two tables, and a footprint for every row",
    "source": "# QFN library — one template, two tables, and a footprint for every row.\n#\n# A template is a function from its parameters to a footprint. This one also\n# names and describes each footprint it makes, by interpolating its parameters\n# into strings, so a table only has to hold the numbers that vary. Columns use\n# the JEDEC MO-220 drawing letters:\n#\n#   n         pin count             e         pitch\n#   D x E     body                  D2 x E2   exposed (thermal) pad\n#   b x L     terminal width x length (b defaults to half the pitch)\n\ntemplate qfn(n, D, D2, e = 0.5, E = D, E2 = D2, b = e / 2, L = 0.4, A = 0.9) {\n  name \"QFN-{n}-1EP_{D}x{E}mm_P{e}mm_EP{D2}x{E2}mm\"\n  description \"QFN, {n} pins, {D} x {E} mm body, {e:.2} mm pitch, {D2} x {E2} mm exposed pad\"\n  refdes \"U\"\n  tags qfn, leadless\n\n  body D x E x A\n  pins n quad pitch e\n  lead flat b x L                     # IPC lands; the span is the body edge\n  pin1 chamfer\n  thermal pad \"{n + 1}\" D2 x E2 {     # the exposed pad is numbered after the last pin\n    paste divide 2 x 2 coverage 65%\n  }\n}\n\n# 0.5 mm pitch: the pitch is fixed for every row, so only n, D and D2 vary.\nfootprints from qfn(e = 0.5) {\n  n    D    D2\n  12   3    1.65\n  16   3    1.7\n  20   4    2.6\n  24   4    2.7\n  28   5    3.35\n  32   5    3.45\n  36   6    4.1\n  40   6    4.6\n  44   7    5.15\n  48   7    5.6\n  56   8    6.0\n  64   9    7.15\n}\n\n# Finer and coarser pitches: any parameter can be a column.\nfootprints from qfn {\n  n    D    e      D2\n  16   4    0.65   2.1\n  24   5    0.65   3.25\n  48   6    0.4    4.6\n  68   8    0.4    6.4\n}\n\n# A single call is named by the template too. This one has a rectangular pad.\nfootprint from qfn(24, 4, 2.45, E2 = 2.65)\n\n# Generated footprints are ordinary footprints: extend one by its name.\nfootprint \"QFN-32-1EP_5x5mm_P0.5mm_EP3.45x3.45mm_HandSolder\" extends \"QFN-32-1EP_5x5mm_P0.5mm_EP3.45x3.45mm\" {\n  description \"QFN-32, 5 x 5 mm, longer terminals for hand soldering\"\n  default pad roundrect 0.25 x 1.0 r 25%\n  courtyard auto 0.5\n}\n"
