    "blurb": "NOT a real part. Four deliberately synthetic footprints that",
    "source": "# syntax_zoo — NOT a real part. Four deliberately synthetic footprints that\n# exercise the constructs the natural examples don't reach, so the whole\n# grammar has runnable coverage. Doubles as a parser test fixture later.\n# Everything below is grammar-valid AND constraint-consistent (no object axis\n# is constrained twice).\n\nunits mil            # file-wide default unit override; suffixes still work\n\nlet big = 200\n\n# --- 1: pad shapes, mask/paste modes, every placement form ------------------\nfootprint \"ZOO-SHAPES\" {\n  description \"grammar coverage fixture; do not manufacture\"\n  manufacturer \"n/a\"\n  mpn \"n/a\"\n\n  pad 1 roundrect 40 x 60 r 25%\n  pad 2 dshape 40 x 60 flat left rotate -90\n  pad 3 oval 40 x 60 mask defined\n  pad 4 rect 40 x 60 paste divide 2 x 2 gutter 8\n  pad 5 circle 30 mask none paste none\n  pad 6 rect 40 x 60 rotate 0.7854rad\n  pad 7 rect 40 x 60\n  pad 8 rect 40 x 60\n  pad 9 rect 40 x 60\n  hole Z1 slot 30 x 55\n\n  pad 1 at (0, 0)\n  pad 2 is 100 right of pad 1                       # x strong; y weak-aligns to pad 1\n  pad 3 is big below pad 2 and 50mil left of pad 2  # and-chain; suffix mid-file\n  pad 4 is 120 right of pad 3\n  align pad 4 with pad 1 horizontally               # strong y replaces the weak default\n  pad 5 is centered between pad 1 and pad 3\n  pad 7 mirrors pad 6 across x                      # pad 6 (prototype) takes +y side\n  gap pad 6 to pad 7 is 70                          # facing edges; axis from the mirror\n  align pad 6 with pad 5 vertically\n  pad 9 mirrors pad 8 across y                      # pad 8 takes the −x side\n  pitch pad 8 to pad 9 is 300\n  align pad 8 with pad 1 horizontally\n  hole Z1 is 80 above pad 1\n}\n\n# --- 2: generator clauses, overrides, graphics, generated-model tweaks ------\nfootprint \"ZOO-DUAL\" {\n  body 200 x 300 x 60\n  pins 10 dual pitch 50 span 260 inner numbering cw pad roundrect 30 x 45 r 8\n  lead jlead 20 x 35\n  density most\n  pin1 bar\n  thermal pad 90 x 140                 # unnamed form (defaults to \"EP\")\n\n  pad 3 { size 34 x 52 }               # partial overrides of generated pads\n  pad 4 { width 40 }\n  pads 6..8 { mask +2 }\n  delete pad 10\n\n  pad \"TP1\" circle 30                  # manual pad coexisting with the generator\n  pad \"TP1\" is 60 left of side left outer\n\n  text ref at (0, 190) size 40\n  text value at (0, -190) size 40 layer assembly\n  silk {\n    outline body offset 6\n    arc (0, 0) r 80 from 30 to 150 width 4\n    circle (0, 120) d 12 fill\n    rect (0, -120) 60 x 20 width 4\n    polygon (90, 90) (110, 90) (100, 110) fill\n  }\n  courtyard rect 320 x 380\n  model {\n    standoff 2\n    height 55\n    body color black\n    leads color tin\n    pin1 dimple\n  }\n}\n\n# --- 3: one-sided part, castellations, `only` -------------------------------\nfootprint \"ZOO-CASTELLATED\" {\n  description \"edge module: castellations along one side\"\n  body 400 x 300 x 40\n  pins 6 single bottom pitch 50\n  lead castellated d 24\n  density least\n  only 1..5                            # keep 1..5, drop position 6\n  pin1 dot\n}\n\n# --- 4: grids with per-axis pitch, layer suppression ------------------------\nfootprint \"ZOO-GRID\" {\n  origin at (0, -25)\n  pins grid 3 x 2 pitch 50 x 80 numbering row-major start bottom-left\n  lead pin d 18\n  default pad tht circle 44 drill 24\n  pad 1 { drill 28 }                   # drill override via block form\n  pads 2..3 { mask -2 }\n  omit 5\n  silk none\n  assembly none\n  courtyard { polygon (-90, -70) (90, -70) (90, 70) (-90, 70) }\n  no model\n}\n"
